            "body": "I also have a patch for #63656 that includes the same `finish_reason` fix and addresses the remaining reported serialization differences:\r\n\r\n- Emit `logprobs: null` when absent.\r\n- Preserve explicit nulls according to chunk type: `token_ids` on content/final choices, and `stop_reason` and `weight_versions` on final choices.\r\n- Include `content: \"\"` in the initial role delta, plus `prompt_token_ids: null` and `prompt_text: null` when unset.\r\n- Omit unset usage details on the usage-only chunk, including `prompt_tokens_details`.\r\n- Include reasoning-token details when a reasoning parser is configured. Without one, omit them from final usage and emit `completion_tokens_details: null` on continuous-usage chunks.\r\n\r\nThe patch also adds HTTP/SSE regression coverage for complete chunk JSON, usage serialization, echo with requested token IDs, and reasoning-parser configuration, plus documentation. All 511 `vllm-server` tests passed using the scripted engine. The separate `system_fingerprint` value difference remains outside its scope.\r\n\r\nAI assistance was used for the implementation and tests. Once this PR is merged, I’ll open a follow-up PR with the remaining changes to fully address #63656.",
